Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: Keep the camera manager responsive during CAMSS PIX start

CAMSS starts the sensor synchronously in VIDIOC_STREAMON. Starting
a front camera on the camera manager thread can block completion of
the rear camera's buffers for longer than the queue can cover.

Prepare and complete the start in the camera manager, but issue the
blocking ioctl from the thread calling Camera::start(). Keep the
public call synchronous and preserve the synchronous start for
pipelines that do not opt in. Close the old video handle on removal
instead of opening a potentially reused node name.

On Xiaomi Pad 8 Pro with two PipeWire clients, starting the front
camera dropped eight rear frames before the change. With split
start the rear delivered 360 consecutive 4K60 buffers, with a
maximum interval of 16.665 ms, and the front delivered all 90 frames.

